  "rationale": "No single non-foothold step is a single point of failure, because the target stays reachable whichever one is blocked. The target is an OR over dbReplica, vaultRead, codeRepo and mailArchive, and these are fed by independent routes. Route A: tokenCache (from the supplychain or wifiGuest footholds) leads to fileServer, then codeRepo, then the target. Route B: apiToken (containerHost AND kerberoast) together with rdpLogin (iotDevice AND workstation) leads to domainAdmin, then mailArchive or dbReplica, then the target. Route C: printServer (via dbLogin or vpnSession) together with monitoringHost (via dbLogin or configSecret) leads to hypervisor, then dbReplica. Route D: rdpLogin together with fileServer leads to secretsManager, then vaultRead, codeRepo or dbReplica. Routes A and B share no intermediate step, so any single block leaves at least one of them intact."
